# =============================================================================
# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon.
#
# Everything not listed here is packed into a tarball and uploaded as the build
# context before the first instruction runs. That has two consequences worth
# understanding:
#
#   1. Speed. target/ after a local build is hundreds of megabytes of class
#      files and a fat jar. Shipping it is pure waste - stage 1 rebuilds from
#      source anyway - and it also busts the layer cache on every build, because
#      the context hash changes whenever any of those files does.
#
#   2. Safety. Anything in the context can be COPYed, deliberately or by
#      accident. A `.env` swept in by a broad `COPY . .` ends up as a readable
#      layer in the published image, and deleting it in a later instruction does
#      NOT remove it - layers are immutable and `docker history` will still show
#      it. The only way a secret stays out of an image is by never entering the
#      context.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
target/
*.jar
*.war
*.class

# ---- Secrets and local configuration ----------------------------------------
# Belt and braces with the root .gitignore: an untracked .env sitting in a
# working copy would still be picked up by the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
**/secrets/

# ---- Version control --------------------------------------------------------
# .git is often the largest thing in the tree and contains every version of
# every file ever committed, including anything that was committed by mistake
# and removed later.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---- IDE and OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Docker's own files -----------------------------------------------------
# Copying the Dockerfile into the image it builds achieves nothing.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ---- Logs and scratch -------------------------------------------------------
*.log
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
